<title>USA: Green Tree Financial raises dividend.</title>
<headline>Green Tree Financial raises dividend.</headline>
<dateline>SAINT PAUL, Minn. 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Green Tree Financial Corp, a financial services company, on Monday said it raised its annual dividend to $0.35 a share from $0.30.</p>
<p>The new rate -- an increase to $0.0875 a quarter from $0.075 -- takes effect in the third quarter of 1997, the company said.</p>
<p>The formal declaration of record and payment dates for the increased quarterly cash dividend is expected to be made when Green Tree reports its second-quarter financial results on July 17, 1997, the company said.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
